"""
## Purpose and audience
Purpose: Prove the round-10 template-elide fast path in
`_html_without_inert_template_sources` returns exactly what the full tag walk
(`_html_without_inert_template_sources_scan`) returns, for every document.
Audience: browser-engine maintainers.

Web-perf round 10 (doc/10_metrics/ui/web_perf_round10_2026-09-13.md) sub-timed
`pp_css_us` for the first time and found this one function carrying 571 ms of
the 892 ms eight-page CSS-parse total -- it walks EVERY tag of the document and
scans each tag name a character at a time in interpreted Simple, in order to
elide `<template>` bodies that most documents do not contain. The fast path
answers "can the walk's `name == "template"` branch fire at all?" and returns
`source` unchanged when it cannot.

That question is the whole spec. The oracle is
`simple_web_layout_debug_template_elide_equivalence(html)`, which runs BOTH the
wrapper and the walk and returns "OK" only when the two results are
byte-identical.

**The first cut (PR #910) got the question wrong and this spec is why the
second one is right.** It probed for the contiguous substring `<template`, but
the walk derives its tag name from `lower.substring(lt + 1, gt).trim()` -- so
`< template>` and `</ template>` reach `name == "template"` with no contiguous
`<template` anywhere, and the fast path returned a document whose template body
the walk elides. Adding those rows made this spec FAIL (`[12] MISMATCH
fast_len=68 slow_len=34`), and the probe was replaced by
`_html_template_tag_present`, which mirrors the walk's own derivation: `<`,
optional whitespace, optionally `/` and more whitespace, then the name.

Coverage is two-tier, the same shape round 9's selector-equivalence spec used:
the eight shared catalog pages give real documents at real scale (all of which
take the fast path), and the adversarial fixtures below give the shapes the
catalog never contains -- a real `<template>` body, nested templates, an
unclosed template, a stray `</template>` with no opener, a template tag inside
a `<script>` body and inside a `<style>` body (where the walk's script/style
skipping means the tag is NOT a template but the probe still fires, so the slow
walk runs and must agree), `<templatex>` (a prefix that is not the tag), a
template whose tag carries attributes, uppercase `<TEMPLATE>`, a tagless
document, the empty document, the three whitespace-in-tag shapes above, and a
document carrying the bare word `template` in prose and in `grid-template`
(which must NOT cost the fast path -- every catalog page contains it, so a
probe on the bare word would delete the whole win).
"""

"""
Traceability: REQ-BROWSER-ENGINE-TEMPLATE-ELIDE-FASTPATH-001 — the template-elide fast path must return exactly what the full tag walk returns.
"""
# @cover src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/browser_engine/simple_web_html_layout_renderer_core.spl 1%
use std.spec.*
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.simple_web_html_layout_renderer_core.{
    simple_web_layout_debug_template_elide_equivalence
}
use std.nogc_sync_mut.fs.{read_file}

val CATALOG = "examples/06_io/ui/web_catalog/"

fn catalog_verdict(page: text) -> text:
    simple_web_layout_debug_template_elide_equivalence(
        read_file(CATALOG + page + ".html")
    )

# Every adversarial shape named in the header, one document per entry. Each is
# run through both paths; any disagreement names the two lengths.
val ADVERSARIAL: [text] = [
    "<html><body><p>no template anywhere</p></body></html>",
    "<html><body><template><p>inert</p></template><p>live</p></body></html>",
    "<html><body><template id=t data-x=\"1\"><p>inert</p></template><b>k</b></body></html>",
    "<html><body><template><template><i>deep</i></template></template><b>k</b></body></html>",
    "<html><body><template><p>never closed</p></body></html>",
    "<html><body></template><p>stray close</p></body></html>",
    "<html><body><script>var s = \"<template>\";</script><p>live</p></body></html>",
    "<html><body><style>/* <template> */ p { color: red; }</style><p>live</p></body></html>",
    "<html><body><templatex><p>not a template</p></templatex></body></html>",
    "<html><body><TEMPLATE><p>upper</p></TEMPLATE><b>k</b></body></html>",
    "plain text with no tags at all",
    "",
    # The shapes that BROKE the first cut of the fast path (PR #910), which
    # probed for the contiguous substring `<template`. The walk derives its tag
    # name from `lower.substring(lt + 1, gt).trim()`, so whitespace after `<`
    # (and between `<` and `/`) still reaches `name == "template"` while the
    # contiguous substring is absent -- the fast path returned the document
    # unchanged where the walk elided a body.
    "<html><body>< template><p>inert</p></template><b>k</b></body></html>",
    "<html><body><\n\ttemplate><p>inert</p></ template><b>k</b></body></html>",
    "<html><body><template><p>inert</p></  template><b>k</b></body></html>",
    # The bare word `template` with no tag before it must NOT cost the fast
    # path: every catalog page contains it (prose and `grid-template`), so a
    # probe on the bare word would delete the whole win.
    "<html><head><style>.g { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }</style></head>" +
        "<body><p>a template is a pattern</p></body></html>"
]

describe "web template-elide fast path equivalence":
    it "agrees with the full tag walk on every catalog page":
        # oracle: every shared catalog document takes the fast path (none of
        # them contains a template tag) and must still produce the walk output.
        expect(catalog_verdict("overview")).to_equal("OK")
        expect(catalog_verdict("html")).to_equal("OK")
        expect(catalog_verdict("css-layout")).to_equal("OK")
        expect(catalog_verdict("css-paint")).to_equal("OK")
        expect(catalog_verdict("forms-media")).to_equal("OK")
        expect(catalog_verdict("animation")).to_equal("OK")
        expect(catalog_verdict("evidence")).to_equal("OK")
        expect(catalog_verdict("tab-bar")).to_equal("OK")

    it "agrees with the full tag walk on every adversarial shape":
        # oracle: real templates, nested, unclosed, stray-close, script/style
        # bodies mentioning the tag, a prefix that is not the tag, uppercase,
        # attributes, a tagless document, the empty document, and the whitespace-in-tag shapes that broke the first cut.
        var mismatches = ""
        var i = 0
        while i < ADVERSARIAL.len():
            val v = simple_web_layout_debug_template_elide_equivalence(
                ADVERSARIAL[i]
            )
            if v != "OK":
                mismatches = "{mismatches} [{i}] {v}"
            i = i + 1
        expect(mismatches).to_equal("")
